    - Dates are compared in the viewer's time zone. Each event's UTC time is converted before the comparison, matching
      how the When column displays it.
    - An end date before the start date shows "The end date must be after the start date." This is checked when you
      leave the field, not on every keystroke.
  - [1mResult count:[0m a "Showing X of 48 events" line, announced to screen readers without moving focus. When nothing
    matches it says "Showing 0 of 48 events". Your notes put a designed empty state out of scope, so there won't be one.
  - [1mWithout JavaScript:[0m the filter bar starts hidden, and the script reveals it. One problem I'm not fixing: the table
    itself is built by JavaScript today, so with JS off the page has no events at all. That breaks your "readable with
    JavaScript disabled" rule. Fixing it means rendering the rows into the HTML, which is its own change. Tell me if you
    want it.

